<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:52:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Canada can offer a more reliable route for energy exports to the EU', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e38829b200ef8bee375a1bf418b196ce536de0a74b29030592c27512de349f2e</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:50:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:42:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-can-offer-a-more-reliable-route-for-energy-exports-to-the-eu-expert-says--5f8600ea249f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/canada-can-offer-a-more-reliable-route-for-energy-exports-to-the-eu-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr. Walaa-Eldeen Bakry, Principal Lecturer in Project Management and Finance and Director of Executive Education at Westminster Business School, says that "Carney is deliberately aiming to diversify the Canadian trade policy", explaining that it "can actually offer a more reliable route in terms of energy exports from Canada into the EU and we have seen last year a significant increase in oil exports to some European countries".</summary></entry><entry><title>'Revolutionary change in American foreign policy': Canada pivoting towards EU, India and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ada526e1442123693761c82dc44e7fbc05eadfb3c552ee3f5f8d2487a874bb41</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:45:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T19:18:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-revolutionary-change-in-american-foreign-policy-canada-pivoting-towards-eu-india-and-china--5811b0689e1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-revolutionary-change-in-american-foreign-policy-canada-pivoting-towards-eu-india-and-china" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Anne Applebaum, staff writer at The Atlantic and author of Autocracy, Inc. According to Applebaum, the upheaval in American diplomacy and foreign policy transcends any one administration. She describes a full-fledged transformation in the way the United States exerts power, pivoting away from leadership of a democratic alliance and toward a transactional, mafia-style politics that fuses ideology, private economic interests, personal relationships and geopolitical leverage.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney seeks closer Europe ties to counter hostile US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cf5b2b32d0c2723bcb4bfd955e88fe35ca42cff44e5b06b37fd43cde2f9aeee</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:45:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T18:57:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/canada-s-carney-seeks-closer-europe-ties-to-counter-hostile-us--1cc68ad20b35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/canada-s-carney-seeks-closer-europe-ties-to-counter-hostile-us" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is heading to Europe in the middle of a trade war with U.S. President Donald Trump, seeking a deeper relationship with the European Union that could give Canadians greater freedom to work and study there. FRANCE 24's Christopher Guly reports from Ottawa.</summary></entry><entry><title>US acknowledges for the first time that it has deployed weapons in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1e0c9f0105c66919ecddc99dfa8289154ac35ea796de1c156161df1e58cab67</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:45:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T18:34:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-acknowledges-for-the-first-time-that-it-has-deployed-weapons-in-space--0f22fd99aebc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/us-acknowledges-for-the-first-time-that-it-has-deployed-weapons-in-space" /><summary type="html">The United States has confirmed for the first time that it has deployed weapons in space, a remarkable revelation after previous warnings about countries such as Russia possibly weaponizing a global frontier long agreed in treaties to be used for only peaceful purposes. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rapid data center expansion incites backlash in Republican stronghold</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10ce03b75f3f00ca84c013411a1b7784a0d6ff95aa90605591bea32b6f4a8dac</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:46:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T15:05:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260915-rapid-data-center-expansion-incites-backlash-in-republican-stronghold--12576b212a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260915-rapid-data-center-expansion-incites-backlash-in-republican-stronghold" /><summary type="html">With just a couple months to go until the US midterm election, a new political fault line is emerging in Republican strongholds across Texas driven by the rapid expansion of artificial intelligence. According to an analysis by the Texas Tribune, nearly 60 percent of planned new data centers are set to be built in congressional districts that voted for Donald Trump in 2024. But the AI boom is now sparking a backlash from some of the voters who helped put him back in office. Pierrick Leurent and Valérie Defert have this report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Corruption ‘endemic’ in Trump administration: 'Checks and balances only in effect at lower courts'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4abf9f7600354a59fb23ccea7fcc3a0f25eba0a5c94c8c6337129a1ee6d70e41</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:46:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:52:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-cour--944e7a2db01b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-courts" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Author, Professor at NYU School of Law, and former General Counsel of the FBI. He argues that as political deception and deliberate falsehoods become normalized, and politically useful, it erodes any trust we have in our government and our institutions. Drawing on his book, "Liar’s Kingdom", Weissmann questions why political leaders are above the law in the United States, while ordinary citizens risk serious legal consequences for making intentionally false statements.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war exposes US munitions shortfall, industrial bottlenecks, Pentagon report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:787bad371003daa32bc2f59fd4933ca9ec9612b6d128d008e0d4b4052d329f2c</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:46:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T06:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says--8ac2e20850a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says" /><summary type="html">The US military faces shortages of key munitions due to the Iran war and industrial "bottlenecks" to rebuild stockpiles, a Pentagon watchdog warned in a report published on Monday, contradicting US President Donald Trump's assurances that ammunition supplies are "virtually unlimited".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy talks in Texas at US invitation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a92cdaf7dd935eea7549cdd930df267e0d0d89c8b5e587c1ae3fafd7b9306ef1</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T02:44:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation--7120fef6df3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation" /><summary type="html">A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d86d5cb8d8231f84ea0118119fc5d587eb79a8b806d9bed75b2b8230beee58f</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins--73bfd34fa579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rapper Macklemore dropped from Ed Sheeran's US tour after pro-Palestinian remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9dacea53b9c59578ca62dce83a73d2c76f415ce4554eb2e807c0e2cfab5090</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks--73709c875802.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks" /><summary type="html">American rapper Macklemore announced Monday that he was dropped from British singer Ed Sheeran’s US stadium tour after saying "Free Palestine" during a September 4 concert in New Jersey. The Grammy winner’s removal follows pressure from venue owners, including New England Patriots owner Robert Kraft, over his criticism of Israel’s actions in Gaza.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Space Force confirms weapons deployed in space for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c681ab3ae9ce5b14d1178cc1072ddd7ca085dcb4809ee196c40b4c986834136f</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:06Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time--b77423806d11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">The US Space Force on Monday confirmed for the first time that Washington has weapons deployed in orbit, as the United States, China and Russia expand their military capabilities in space. The disclosure highlights a growing focus on controlling the space domain and protecting satellites vital to military communications, surveillance and navigation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump criticises 'negative forces' seeking to slow AI development</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab39970ca5454309c78c21256838b0fa93a80ccf27cf436c1355fb7f1cb0e6e1</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:49:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development--bd4a498a26cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-trump-criticises-negative-forces-seeking-to-slow-ai-development" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday slammed critics of artificial intelligence (AI) who warned firms to slow down development, branding them "negative" forces. The comments came soon after OpenAI CEO Sam Altman announced his company will not go public this year, citing safety concerns.</summary></entry><entry><title>US hosts G20 energy talks in Texas as Iran war disrupts global fuel markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc015af21fdc93fb2553355ddf50cf995ae8f7db86ab6fedfba4eb30abeaa785</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T01:42:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-g20-energy-talks-iran-war--39ce092f6892.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-g20-energy-talks-iran-war" /><summary type="html">The United States begins G20 meetings in Houston on Monday promoting “energy abundance” as President Donald Trump’s war against Iran disrupts global fuel markets. Delegations from major economies, including China, India, Japan and Germany, will attend alongside oil producers Canada and Saudi Arabia. Russia is also expected to participate.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘I gave up my life to care for my father’: How 9/11 shaped a son’s sense of duty and life trajectory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3555e559afd25f862e10fb249cf2c8019b8992051b63d3dad0647cde12bf34c9</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T17:10:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/i-gave-up-my-life-to-care-for-my-father-how-9-11-shaped-a-son-s-sense-of-duty-and-life-trajectory--da02b8721d79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/i-gave-up-my-life-to-care-for-my-father-how-9-11-shaped-a-son-s-sense-of-duty-and-life-trajectory" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Alessandro Stravato, a witness to the attacks of September 11th. His testimony offers a deeply personal account. He witnessed firsthand the second plane strike the World Trade Center from Arthur Ashe Stadium. Stravato’s first instinct was not to interpret the historical significance, just find his father, who was working at City Hall.  He found him alive, covered in debris and soot, trekking dozens of blocks through Manhattan. And while his father did survive, his health seriously deteriorated over the years. By 2015, as Alessandro's dad was losing his battle with cancer, he told his son to "stay strong."</summary></entry><entry><title>‘We did what we had to do’: 25 years on, 9/11 first responder reflects on duty, survival and family</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8547aee8b4b661a9fae437730e975356fdd997ae0f068bbcf95db624aa54d515</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T16:18:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/we-did-what-we-had-to-do-25-years-on-9-11-first-responder-reflects-on-duty-survival-and-family--5b4d9acc4527.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/we-did-what-we-had-to-do-25-years-on-9-11-first-responder-reflects-on-duty-survival-and-family" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome LaZetta Duncan, Retired NYPD Detective, 9/11 First Responder. Duncan remembers Ground Zero not as a historical event frozen in time, but as living history whose consequences continue to unfold and evolve 25 years on. Her testimony traces a striking progression: from the confusion and urgency of the attacks, rescue and recovery, to the grim transformation of gathering human remains and evidence inside a burning toxic apocalyptic crime scene. And we now learn of the overwhelming health consequences borne by responders despite repeated assurances that the air quality posed no health threat.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c4c3c6aa862df5f9bcd577b3101e2a2586f83268afa684077ba3b6222000dda</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race--c6d331e45ad7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9cefa906b64b85328595def7b49745a1daf8b1fec13abe1ca1bb8d33058dc14</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T10:48:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive--652ff4e85a45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images, from commemorations marking 25 years since the 9/11 attacks to the breakthrough win for Germany's far-right AfD party and the lightening offensive that has left Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels in control of the country's Red Sea coast.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Carney to visit North Atlantic French islands after Trump's map post</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4d139182a19b55903df96489c7b10dd6a46f22f799d74f31cd6ea1572c4eced</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post--f17f71093187.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney will reaffirm the “sovereignty of nations” on a visit on September 20 to Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory in the North Atlantic, the Élysée Palace announced on Sunday. The symbolic trip comes after US President Donald Trump posted a map on social media showing the entire North American continent covered by the US flag.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>On Sept 12th, 'everyone was compassionate': The world needs 'to be together again' - Richard Roeill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94004352322065408207e78810ebb36816609c21324f16f58d1cda55c6f8c2e3</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T07:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill--bad1381d87fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24’s François Picard talks to Richard Roeill, former New York Firefighter and 9/11 First Responder. Roeill’s testimony reframes the legacy of September 11th not as a historical event confined to a single day, but as living history. The former New York City firefighter describes an anniversary that reactivates trauma, while the illnesses suffered by first responders make the consequences of Ground Zero ever-present decades later. He says that responders were misled about the dangers they faced and demands accountability and long-term healthcare for those exposed to the toxic air.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Can we slow down AI, and who has the right to remember 9/11?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a405c1b27ee801dac30cf154ac0161baf34a7b2d2651163001a93c3100f1ccc5</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T18:43:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember--b55b74262dd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember" /><summary type="html">In a week that marks 25 years since 9/11, Americans paused to pay tribute. Six bells tolled to signify six fatal moments in New York, at the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania– with a seventh bell rung this year to commemorate those who later died from 9/11-related illnesses.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>US government has decided on 'Guantanamo forever'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62b2a247f842ec2af80f1836f35e7afe5eb6bca50ca96c591b1de90d8147e69a</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T18:42:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight--86e38a56a856.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight" /><summary type="html">In this edition, FRANCE 24’s Gavin Lee speaks to New York Times reporter Carol Rosenberg, widely regarded as one of the foremost American journalists covering the US detention camp at Guantanamo Bay in Cuba. Several alleged suspects in the 9/11 attacks are still being held there, including their so-called “architect”, Khalid Sheikh Mohammed. He is scheduled for trial in June 2028, 27 years after the tragedy. To mark the anniversary, Rosenberg has written a reflective piece titled A Place Where Memories Have Faded Away.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro probed for corruption as Brazil election tightens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5506522ee4e2a606a271b42b8480a5e9fab645dc2f6dd889e3ce9675ee49e6a1</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T16:21:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-flavio-bolsonaro-probed-for-corruption-as-brazil-election-tightens--7d6742f29229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-flavio-bolsonaro-probed-for-corruption-as-brazil-election-tightens" /><summary type="html">Just weeks before the vote, Brazilian presidential hopeful Flavio Bolsonaro's campaign is being rocked by revelations he is under investigation for alleged corruption and money laundering. The probe centres on financing sought for a film about his father, former president Jair Bolsonaro, court documents unsealed on Friday showed.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump delivers remarks at Pentagon ceremony to mark 25th anniversary of 9/11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3e33f03fc61632bea10ca0fc91920125b548cee6cd27978c9e0a009091a882e</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T15:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-trump-delivers-remarks-at-pentagon-ceremony-to-mark-25th-anniversary-of-9-11--e6337c0b2900.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-trump-delivers-remarks-at-pentagon-ceremony-to-mark-25th-anniversary-of-9-11" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump observed Friday’s 25th anniversary by speaking about 9/11 at a ceremony at the Pentagon commemorating the lives lost when al-Qaeda militants hijacked planes and killed nearly 3,000 people in three locations, upending American foreign policy and national security.</summary></entry><entry><title>25 years after 9/11, al Qaeda remains a threat – even as Washington looks away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3eb9021d3a0238823a06294c5d3a575cf224e856dc621f9b1075221c42b5d634</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:24:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-remains-threat-washington-looks-away-counter-terrorism--04413861dca2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-remains-threat-washington-looks-away-counter-terrorism" /><summary type="html">A quarter of a century after the deadliest terrorist attacks in US history, al Qaeda’s various branches have moved away from the global jihad advocated by Osama bin Laden, focusing instead on regional insurgencies. Their actions continue to destabilise swathes of the world, from the Sahel to Afghanistan, neglected by a US administration that critics say has unlearned the lessons of 9/11.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>How the media has changed since 9/11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba574f214cea960dcbdad3da2616a3191db817065afce230fc204655d7976562</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T13:37:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260911-how-the-media-has-changed-since-9-11--edf3bd4e39ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260911-how-the-media-has-changed-since-9-11" /><summary type="html">It has been 25 years since terrorists hijacked planes and flew them into the Twin Towers, the Pentagon, and a fourth crashed in a field in Pennsylvania. Nearly 3,000 people were killed in the attacks that changed the course of US and world history. This week FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at how journalists covered 9/11 and how the attacks changed the news industry.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>Vance calls Democrats 'party of hatred' as he seizes MAGA spotlight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:701b8095d6b16fdbbb6a24bafbeb3e1a98cc3aa5fc533454a6e67fba173e2f90</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:45:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-vance-tries-label-democrats-as-party-of-hatred-seizes-maga-spotlight--9c4acb879556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-vance-tries-label-democrats-as-party-of-hatred-seizes-maga-spotlight" /><summary type="html">US Vice President JD Vance launched a virulent attack on the Democratic Party Thursday, accusing them of being the "party of hatred" at day two of the Republican convention ahead of the November midterm elections. With public support for President Donald Trump at record lows, Republican figures are increasingly trying to frame their opponents as dangerous political extremists.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'That's why we fight': The US marks 25 years since 9/11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16a81de7fa8991f438769368aa0c6de4df61e371e7e1c654069a609a562d168d</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:51:54Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T01:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor--1ab77d9771b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor" /><summary type="html">New York on Friday marked the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001 attacks, with US President Donald Trump attending a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents joined commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e57a0dc4ce0e8f9bbd055620d942c951f9131fd6950ad1d9a39ceed2a9304cc</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:11:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1--ff193be16a97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1" /><summary type="html">Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1077818961e451d138ebaba56ac1d95502aef025e3145fb0c16735820dd087b</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:44:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks--138f5fff2da5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>9/11 then and now: Do September 2001 attacks still shape our world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a44dcc636b9cc533b7f53e7389010813d23df1d6ea3edca27d91bb7c6ec894d1</id><updated>2026-09-15T19:52:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T18:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world--b22b4497a9ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world" /><summary type="html">Once in a generation – sometimes once in a lifetime – a singular event blindsides the entire planet. 25 years on, does the memory of the 9/11 attacks on New York's Twin Towers, the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania fade into history, or is it still as raw and vivid as on that sunny September morning?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry></feed>
